Translation patch: `ComStmtExecuteRequestBuilder::build` and `MySerialize for ComStmtExecuteRequest` (loops)

Change: `for (i, param) in params.iter().enumerate()` becomes `for i in 0..params.len()` using `params[i]`, over the input slice (the `collect` into `Vec<&Value>` moves after the loop). `for param in &self.params` becomes `for i in 0..self.params.len() { let param: &Value = self.params[i]; .. }`, with `**param` becoming `*param`.
Why: Aeneas does not model `Enumerate` or the slice and `Vec` iterators (see patches 04/05).
Behaviour: Identical: the same elements are visited in the same order. `collect` only builds a vector of references to the same elements.

